        "original_id": "39d96245-e12f-5211-b2ea-88de87f9cb4d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Ontario Raiders, Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment, Toronto Maple Leafs, Toronto Blue Jays, Toronto Rock\n- People: Tie Domi, Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Bobby Orr, Max Domi\n- Places: Toronto, Maple Leaf Gardens\n- Roles: Assistant General Manager, president, player\n\nFacts:\n- Tie Domi was born on November 1, 1969.\n- Tie Domi is a retired Canadian professional ice hockey player of Albanian origin.\n- Bill Watters was the Assistant General Manager of the Toronto Maple Leafs when a group bought the Ontario Raiders.\n- Paul Beeston was the former president of the Toronto Blue Jays when a group bought the Ontario Raiders.\n- Tie Domi was a player for the Toronto Maple Leafs when a group bought the Ontario Raiders.\n- Bobby Orr was a former NHL player when a group bought the Ontario Raiders.\n- Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment considered purchasing the Ontario Raiders but did not complete the purchase.\n- A group including Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Tie Domi, and Bobby Orr bought the Ontario Raiders for $250,000.\n- The new owners promptly relocated the Ontario Raiders to Toronto's Maple Leaf Gardens and rebranded the team as the Toronto Rock.\n- Max Domi's father is former Toronto Maple Leafs player Tie Domi.",
